# a bass track plays LOW and ONE note at a time: a white key (CHORDS) used to send a four-note stack into the one-voice
# SOFTBASS, which kept only the top of it (E5, 659 Hz); and the keys started at C4. Now: the key's root, two octaves down
wait 300
tap HOME
wait 100
tapkey w3
wait 100
tap HOME
wait 100
expect track 3
expect eng 4
key w0 down 100
wait 200
expect voices 1
expect_out USB 93 1D 63
key w0 up
wait 800
tapkey b0
wait 200
expect_out USB 93 18 63
wait 800
# OCT lifts it by an octave, and the other tracks keep their chords
trkoct 1
key w0 down 100
wait 200
expect_out USB 93 29 63
key w0 up
wait 500
tap HOME
wait 100
tapkey w0
wait 100
tap HOME
wait 100
expect track 0
key w0 down 100
wait 200
expect_out USB 90 35 63
expect voices >1
key w0 up
wait 300
